course: dictionary
lesson: 101
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word address has more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one is meant. «Zara's online friend offered a gift card if she told him her address.» Here address means the place where someone lives, or where they can be found.
explain: Address can also be a doing word, a verb. «Address the class» means speak to the whole class. «Address the issue» means deal with a problem.
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the words around the word. A letter or parcel needs an address on it, and a formal speech can also be called an address. Ask which meaning fits, then try it in the sentence to check.
fact: Address means the details of where a person or building is: house number, street, town and postcode.
fact: «An address goes in this order: the name, then house number and street, then town or city, then state or county, then postcode or ZIP code.»
fact: Address can also mean an email or website address, which tells you where to find something online.
fact: As a verb, address means to speak to someone or a group, or to write the address on a letter or parcel.
fact: «The most important words you can say are your address, which is why learning it by heart is a real safety skill.» Never give your address to strangers or post it online.
exercise: «Zara's online friend offered a gift card if she told him her address.» Should Zara share her address with him? | Yes, because he is her friend | Yes, but only by posting it on the class website | Yes, if he offers a gift card | *No, never give your address to a stranger online
exercise: «Address the class.» What does address mean here? | Copy the class list into a book | Lock the classroom door | *Speak to the whole class | Write the class name on a letter
exercise: «An address goes in this order: the name, then house number and street.» Which part comes first? | *The name | House number | Postcode | Town or city
test: «Please address this parcel to Grandma.» What does address mean here? | Speak to Grandma loudly | *Write her address on the parcel | Open the parcel and look inside | Wrap the parcel in paper
test: Why is learning your address by heart a safety skill? | *So you can tell a helper where you live if you get lost | So you can make your name longer | So you can post it online for your friends | So you can write faster on an envelope
exam: Which meaning of address fits «the principal's keynote address to the school»? | A house number and street | A website link | Writing on an envelope | *A formal speech given to a group
